#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""xiv-arcade: the host side of XivDesktop's /arcade.

Indexes the game files YOU put in your games folder, starts them in RetroArch, and keeps every
battery save and save state in one directory tree that Syncthing replicates between your machines.

It never downloads, links to or searches for ROMs, disc images or BIOS files. Bring your own dumps
of games you own. Python 3.9+, standard library only; runs with or without the game.

  xiv-arcade setup            create the folders, READMEs, RetroArch overrides and the database
  xiv-arcade scan             re-index the games folder
  xiv-arcade list             what is in the library
  xiv-arcade launch NAME      fuzzy-launch (add --dry-run to print the exact command and stop)
  xiv-arcade last             resume the most recent game
  xiv-arcade setup --launchbox DIR   also read a LaunchBox folder where it lives
  xiv-arcade import-saves DIR copy saves from another RetroArch install, never over a newer save
  xiv-arcade sync             force a save sync and show its status
  xiv-arcade sync-setup       print (or --apply) the Syncthing folder configuration
  xiv-arcade pair [DEVICE-ID] print this device's id, or the commands that pair another one
"""
